TRON does not actually calculate separate H1, M15 and M5 dashboard states internally. The dashboard is populated from the current chart timeframe, while it separately pulls M5 RSI/EMA and H4/H1 session data. The script is optimized for M1/M5 and limits the drawing layer around 15m.
So when we use your H1 → M15 → M5 templates, we are externalizing the same TRON engine by reading it on those chart timeframes, not pretending the dashboard itself contains four independent timeframe dashboards.
That is exactly how I would build this.

