The actual underlying engine uses:
RSI length = 10
Bullish threshold = 55
Bearish threshold = 48
Overbought exhaustion = 85
Oversold exhaustion = 20.
Telegram dictionary
🟢 RSI Momentum = Bullish
→ Buying momentum state is active.

🔴 RSI Momentum = Bearish
→ Selling momentum state is active.

⚪ RSI Momentum = Neutral
→ No active bullish/bearish momentum state.

🚨 RSI ≥ 85
→ Bullish momentum has reached the configured exhaustion boundary.

🚨 RSI ≤ 20
→ Bearish momentum has reached the configured exhaustion boundary.
One subtle but important detail: the actual bearish condition requires RSI < 48, RSI > 20, and falling RSI EMA; the bullish condition requires RSI to cross above 55, remain below 85, and have rising RSI EMA.
So don't reduce TRON to a generic RSI rule.

